
This utility will allow the dumping an AO seg index table associated with a given AO table with indexes.

The aoseghistory.tar tar file contains the following files.

  README                - This file.
  gp_aoseg_history.so   - The shared library that contains a psql function.


To use:

  * Copy the aoseghistory.so library file to each host in the cluster. For example,

    gpscp -f hosts aoseghistory.so =:$GPHOME/lib   


  * Create a postgres function reference. You'll need to create the reference on the segment if you intend
    to connect to the segment and reference the function. For example,

    PGOPTIONS=' -c gp_session_role=utility ' psql mydatabase -p 51000
    
    CREATE FUNCTION my_gp_aoseg_history(oid)
      RETURNS TABLE( 
        gp_tid tid
      , gp_xmin integer
      , gp_xmin_status text
      , gp_xmin_commit_distrib_id text
      , gp_xmax integer
      , gp_xmax_status text
      , gp_xmax_commit_distrib_id text
      , gp_command_id integer
      , gp_infomask text
      , gp_update_tid tid
      , gp_visibility text
      , segno integer
      , tupcount bigint
      , eof bigint
      , eof_uncompressed bigint
      ) 
    AS '<location of gp_aoseg_history.so file>', 'gp_aoseg_history_wrapper' LANGUAGE C STRICT;


  * Get the Oid of the table you are interested in.

    SELECT oid FROM pg_class WHERE relname = '<table name>';


  * Call the function using the table's oid.

    SELECT * FROM my_gp_aoseg_history(<table's oid>);



